This archive is now HISTORY: WpLock.v in the tree IS the flipped file, the
27-site creator sweep is in, ProofInitlock mints at its own store, and the
blocker below (ProofPipeclose:749) was dissolved by the §0.26' restatement
(A6.85) -- kfree_pre is KallocInv.page_free now, so the wpay cell never has
to re-enter the ctx tower.  DO NOT RE-APPLY wplock_new.py; it will fail its
own asserts.  Three manual steps it does NOT do are recorded in A6.86 §(1),
and one of its notes below is off by a name (there is no `lock_body`).

THE M4 CONTRACT FLIP, ARCHIVED (tso-machine-flip.md A6.84).

wplock_new.py  -- the WpLock half, applied to the file as A6.83 left it.
                  IT COMPILED GREEN: lock_word at phys_ledger_word4, the
                  owner cell at the wpay payload with the own-invariant,
                  the two address claims in lock_inv, all four creators,
